version: 2

models:

- name: gold_dim_customer
  description: "Customer dimension table in the GOLD layer containing one record per
    Alpenstrom customer. It consolidates descriptive attributes about each customer,
    including segmentation (residential, SME, industrial), industry classification,
    geographic location across Swiss cantons and language regions, and contractual
    details such as tariff, contract type, start date, contracted power capacity and
    current status. This table is intended to support customer analytics, segmentation
    and reporting when joined with fact tables covering consumption, billing and emissions."
  columns:
  - name: customer_id
    description: "Unique identifier assigned to each customer (e.g. 'CUST_0001').
      Used as the key for joining with fact tables containing consumption, billing
      or contract activity."
  - name: customer_name
    description: "Full legal or personal name of the customer. For business customers
      this includes the company name and legal form (e.g. SA, Sàrl, AG); for residential
      customers it contains the individual's name."
  - name: customer_type
    description: "High-level customer segment indicating the nature of the account.
      Observed values include 'Residential', 'SME' (small and medium-sized enterprises)
      and 'Industrial'."
  - name: industry
    description: "Industry or sector in which the customer operates (e.g. 'Paper &
      Packaging', 'Hospitality', 'Data Centers'). For residential customers the value
      is 'Household'."
  - name: canton
    description: "Full name of the Swiss canton where the customer is located (e.g.
      'Ticino', 'Vaud', 'Zurich'). Used for geographic analysis across Switzerland."
  - name: canton_code
    description: "Two-letter official abbreviation of the Swiss canton (e.g. 'TI',
      'VD', 'ZH', 'BE', 'BS'). Convenient for compact reporting and geographic grouping."
  - name: city
    description: "City or municipality where the customer is located (e.g. 'Lugano',
      'Zürich', 'Bern')."
  - name: language_region
    description: "Primary language region of Switzerland associated with the customer's
      location. Observed values include 'German-speaking', 'French-speaking' and 'Italian-speaking'."
  - name: contract_type
    description: "Type of energy supply contract the customer has signed, such as
      'Fixed'. Describes the pricing or commitment structure of the agreement."
  - name: tariff_id
    description: "Identifier of the tariff plan applied to the customer (e.g. 'TRF_IND_FIX',
      'TRF_SME_GRN', 'TRF_RES_FIX'). Encodes the customer segment and tariff variant."
  - name: contract_start_date
    description: "Date on which the customer's current energy supply contract became
      effective."
  - name: contracted_power_kw
    description: "Contracted peak power capacity for the customer, expressed in kilowatts
      (kW). Reflects the maximum power level agreed in the contract and typically
      scales with customer type (small for residential, larger for SME and industrial
      customers)."
  - name: customer_status
    description: "Current lifecycle status of the customer account, for example 'Active'.
      Used to distinguish active customers from inactive or terminated ones."

- name: gold_dim_date
  description: "Date dimension table for the Alpenstrom GOLD layer, providing standardized
    calendar attributes used to analyze energy consumption, demand, and billing trends
    over time. It enables slicing of facts by year, quarter, month, and season, which
    is particularly relevant for Swiss energy analytics where seasonal patterns strongly
    influence demand."
  columns:
  - name: date
    description: "Calendar date representing a specific day. Serves as the time reference
      for joining with fact tables in the GOLD layer."
  - name: year
    description: "Calendar year associated with the date, used for year-over-year
      comparisons of energy metrics."
  - name: quarter
    description: "Calendar quarter label (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4) corresponding to the date,
      used for quarterly reporting and trend analysis."
  - name: month
    description: "Numeric month of the year (1 through 12) extracted from the date,
      useful for monthly aggregations and sorting."
  - name: month_name
    description: "Full English name of the month (e.g., January, April) associated
      with the date, intended for human-readable reports and dashboards."
  - name: season
    description: "Season label (e.g., Spring, Summer, Autumn, Winter) assigned to
      the date, supporting seasonal analysis of energy consumption and demand patterns
      in Switzerland."

- name: gold_dim_energy_tariff
  description: "Dimension table in the GOLD layer describing the energy tariffs offered
    by Alpenstrom to its Swiss customers. Each row represents a distinct tariff product,
    including its commercial name, target customer segment, pricing structure, and
    reference price in CHF per MWh. This table supports conversational analytics on
    tariff portfolios, pricing comparisons across customer types, and revenue segmentation
    by tariff category."
  columns:
  - name: tariff_id
    description: "Unique identifier for each tariff product (e.g. TRF_RES_FIX). Used
      to reference tariffs across other models in the warehouse."
  - name: tariff_name
    description: "Commercial name of the tariff as marketed to customers (e.g. 'Alpenstorm
      Home Fix', 'Alpenstorm Business Flex')."
  - name: customer_type
    description: "Customer segment the tariff is designed for, such as Residential
      (private households) or SME (small and medium enterprises)."
  - name: tariff_category
    description: "Pricing structure category of the tariff. Observed values include
      'Fixed' (price guaranteed over a defined period) and 'Variable' (market-indexed,
      periodically reviewed)."
  - name: price_per_mwh
    description: "Reference price of the tariff expressed in CHF per MWh of energy
      consumed."
  - name: description
    description: "Human-readable description of the tariff, outlining its key commercial
      characteristics such as pricing mechanism, energy source, or target customer."

- name: gold_fact_energy_consumption
  description: "Gold-layer fact table recording periodic energy consumption events
    for Alpenstrom customers. Each row represents the energy delivered to a specific
    customer under a specific tariff for a given date, along with associated financial
    metrics (in CHF), peak demand (in kW), and carbon emissions (in metric tons).
    This table supports analytics on consumption patterns, revenue, cost, and environmental
    impact across customers, tariffs, and time periods."
  columns:
  - name: consumption_id
    description: "Unique identifier for each energy consumption record in the fact
      table."
  - name: customer_id
    description: "Identifier of the Alpenstrom customer associated with the consumption
      event. Can be used to join with the customer dimension."
  - name: date
    description: "Reference date of the consumption record, typically representing
      the start of the billing or measurement period."
  - name: tariff_id
    description: "Identifier of the tariff plan applied to the consumption record
      (e.g., industrial fixed, residential variable). Can be used to join with the
      tariff dimension."
  - name: consumption_mwh
    description: "Total energy consumed by the customer during the period, measured
      in megawatt-hours (MWh)."
  - name: peak_demand_kw
    description: "Maximum power demand observed for the customer during the period,
      measured in kilowatts (kW)."
  - name: price_per_mwh
    description: "Unit price applied to the customer's consumption during the period,
      expressed in CHF per MWh."
  - name: energy_cost_chf
    description: "Cost incurred by Alpenstrom to supply the energy for this consumption
      record, expressed in Swiss francs (CHF)."
  - name: revenue_chf
    description: "Revenue generated from the customer for the energy consumed during
      the period, expressed in Swiss francs (CHF)."
  - name: co2_emissions_tons
    description: "Carbon dioxide emissions attributed to the energy consumed during
      the period, expressed in metric tons."
